//! fraccional-googleworkspace-mcp core: maps the person's selection to a `gws` login, reports status,
//! revokes access, exports agent skills and writes the Install prompt.
//!
//! The whole behaviour sits behind [`Core`], built from injected [`Paths`] and two ports,
//! [`ProcessRunner`] and [`HttpClient`]. Each ticket owns one module and adds its
//! `impl Core { ... }` block there, so tickets do not edit this file.
//!
//! | Module | Ticket | Provides |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | [`scopes`] | T02 | selection <-> scopes, defaults, UI catalogue |
//! | [`gws_binary`] | T03 | `Core::find_gws`, `Core::ensure_gws` |
//! | [`system_http`] | T03 | real [`HttpClient`] |
//! | [`settings`] | T04 | `Core::settings`, `set_config_dir`, `set_key_storage` |
//! | [`gws_env`] | T04 | `Core::gws_command`, credential and marker helpers |
//! | [`status`] | T05 | `Core::status` |
//! | [`revoke`] | T06 | `Core::revoke_all` |
//! | [`save`] | T07 | `Core::save`, `Core::cancel_login` |
//! | [`skills`] | T08 | `Core::export_skills_zip`, `skills::skills_add_command` |
//! | [`mcp`] | MCP | `mcp::serve`: the `gws`, `status` and `open_fraccional_googleworkspace_mcp` tools over MCP stdio |
//! | [`mcp_clients`] | MCP | `mcp_clients::install_prompt`, the Install prompt for an Agent, and `check_exe_path` |
//! | [`mcp_extension`] | MCP | `mcp_extension::mcp_extension`, the `.mcpb` MCP extension for Claude Desktop |
//!
//! Conventions for those tickets: put tests in `crates/core/tests/<module>.rs` using
//! `testing::FakeRunner`, `testing::FakeHttp` and temp dirs; drop the `should_panic`
//! marker from a stub's doc example once it is implemented.
//!
//! # Example
//!
//! ```no_run
//! use fraccional_googleworkspace_mcp_core::{Core, Paths};
//! let core = Core::system(Paths { home: "/home/ana".into(), app_data: "/home/ana/.fraccional".into() });
//! let status = core.status();
//! ```

